// The control plane and the SDK it is developed against, which now live in
// different repositories.
//
// They cannot be one module: the control plane is BUSL-1.1 and the SDK is
// Apache-2.0, and the boundary between them has to be the gRPC contract in
// proto/ rather than a package import. But they are still written together --
// the control plane's own tests drive the SDK against a real server over
// bufconn, which is worth considerably more than testing a mirror against a
// stub -- so development wants both trees editable at once.
//
// This assumes moqom-go is checked out beside this repository, which is where
// it lands if you cloned both into the same directory. It is required rather
// than convenient: moqom-go has no published tag yet, so there is no version
// for the network to resolve, and go/go.mod carries a matching `replace` for
// anyone building with GOWORK=off. Both go away at the first release.
go 1.26.0

use (
	../moqom-go
	./go
)
